' Today's execute-then-merge pipeline on a protocol-6 (v6) shard, at
' feature/cost-accounted-rho e38ff0de8 (dev 93e38575e merged). Each step
' carries the file:line of the code that performs it, at that commit. The
' audit of 2026-10-12 corrected the merge, play and replay steps.
'
' The diagram marks the two places where run-to-completion lives (the block
' play and the validator replay before acceptance) and the two places where
' the merge runs (the proposer before play, and every validator before replay).
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-consensus-proposal.md §3.
' Palette: user and envelope = supply blue · proposer = control amber ·
'   merge = surface salmon · execution and replay = pool green ·
'   validation and finality = capability indigo ·
'   run-to-completion and merge hot spots = red note
' The legend also defines every name and abbreviation that the labels use,
' so the diagram reads on its own.
' Render:  ./render.sh consensus-proposal-today-pipeline.puml
'          (or: plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/consensus-proposal-today-pipeline.puml)

@startuml consensus-proposal-today-pipeline
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor              $ca_neutral
  LifeLineBorderColor     #666666
  ParticipantBorderColor  #333333
  DividerBackgroundColor  $ca_note_grey
  GroupBorderColor        #666666
}
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
title Today: execute-then-merge on a v6 shard (HEAD e38ff0de8)

autonumber

actor       "User\n(signer)"                                    as U  $ca_supply
participant "Proposer\nblock_creator.rs"                        as P  $ca_control
participant "Merge\ninterpreter_util.rs\ndag_merger.rs\nconflict_set_merger.rs" as M $ca_surface
participant "Play runtime\nrholang/runtime.rs\noffered_block.rs"  as R  $ca_pool
participant "Validator\nvalidation_dispatcher.rs\ninterpreter_util.rs" as V $ca_capability
participant "Replay\nruntime_manager.rs"                        as RP $ca_pool
participant "Finalizer\nfinalization_runner.rs\nclique_oracle.rs" as F $ca_capability

== Proposal ==
U -[$ca_instantiate]> P : signed offered envelope\nbody, funding_intent, phloLimit, phloPrice\n(offered.rs:11-21)
P -> P : select at most one offer,\nthe rest become alternates\n(block_creator.rs:1847-1916)
P -> M : compute_parents_post_state\n(interpreter_util.rs:932-942)
M -> M : read the event-log index of the scope.\nv6: compose a conflict-free scope, else\none ordered pass, after execution\n(interpreter_util.rs:1995-2036)
M --> P : merged pre-state, rejected records,\napplied-from-scope, merge base
note over P, M $ca_note_red
  **Merge before execution.** The proposer cannot run
  a deploy until it has merged the parents' post-states.
end note
P -> R : compute_state_envelopes\n(runtime.rs:327-392)
R -> R : check the funding at R0\n(offered_block.rs:220-236), execute,\nthen settle (offered_block.rs:259-280)
R -> R : producer self-replay of the same envelope\n(offered_block.rs:315-323)
R -> R : system deploys, CloseBlock\n(offered_block.rs:361-370)
note right of R $ca_note_red
  **Run-to-completion.** A v6 block holds one envelope
  (runtime.rs:346). A second envelope is an error
  (runtime.rs:364-373). The legacy loop plays each
  deploy to termination (runtime.rs:455-476).
end note
R --> P : post-state root, processed deploy
P -[$ca_instantiate]> V : broadcast the signed block

== Validation by every validator ==
V -> V : block summary and offered-only check\n(validation_dispatcher.rs:99-130)
V -> M : recompute the merge from the block's parents\n(interpreter_util.rs:420-435)
M --> V : computed pre-state, records, state facts
V -> V : compare pre-state, rejected records and\nstate facts (interpreter_util.rs:463-534)
V -> RP : replay_block (interpreter_util.rs:540-547)
RP -> RP : a legacy block waits for the one-permit\nReplayLock (runtime_manager.rs:198-205, 1227).\nAn offered replay takes none (:1317-1333)\nand first checks the funding at R0 (replay.rs:1642)
RP -> RP : replay the envelope and system deploys\nto termination
RP --> V : replayed post-state equals the block's?
note over V, RP $ca_note_red
  **Acceptance waits for execution.** A validator accepts
  a block only after it has recomputed the merge and
  replayed the block (interpreter_util.rs:402-557).
end note
V -> V : eager merge index when the shard\nallows more than one parent\n(validation_dispatcher.rs:340-375)
V -> F : add the valid block to the DAG

== Finality ==
F -> F : every finalization_rate blocks, derive the floor\nof the live view and adopt it as LFB\n(finalization_runner.rs:493-560, 662-701)
F -> F : weight map from the main parent's bonds,\nwhich execution wrote into the block\n(clique_oracle.rs:202-220)

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| user and signed envelope |
  |<$ca_control>| proposer |
  |<$ca_surface>| post-hoc merge analysis |
  |<$ca_pool>| execution and replay |
  |<$ca_capability>| validation, DAG and finality (Casper core) |
  |<$ca_note_red>| run-to-completion and merge hot spots |

  |= name |= meaning |
  | HEAD e38ff0de8 | the commit of feature/cost-accounted-rho that this diagram shows |
  | v6 shard | a shard of protocol version 6: cost accounting, offered envelopes only |
  | offered envelope | a signed user deploy: body, funding intent, phlo limit, phlo price |
  | R0 | the original root: the authenticated state root that a candidate funds from |
  | CloseBlock | the system deploy that closes each block |
  | ReplayLock | a semaphore with one permit: a node replays one legacy block at a time |
  | DAG | the directed acyclic graph of blocks |
  | LFB | the last finalized block |
  | floor | the highest ancestor that the clique oracle certifies as finalized |
  | file.rs:a-b | lines a to b of a source file at HEAD |
endlegend

@enduml
